WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:06.350
. We have a new report out that seeks to answer
the question how many coronavirus deaths can

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:09.040
we really attribute to former President Donald
Trump?

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:13.759
And, you know, one of the things we knew intuitively
during the Trump presidency and which was

00:00:13.759 --> 00:00:19.260
confirmed a number of times by different studies,
was that no president could have predicted

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.670
every coronavirus death.

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:25.500
No president could have even prevented rather
rather than predicted predicted is a different

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.500
thing.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.740
No president could have prevented every coronavirus
death.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.560
We were going to have many deaths as even
countries that dealt with the virus well had

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:35.160
many deaths.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:40.430
But the lack of taking the virus seriously
by the Trump administration from day one certainly

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:44.300
was at least partially responsible for some
of the deaths.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:51.850
A new report now says that 40 percent of the
deaths that took place in 2020 could have

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:57.500
been avoided if Trump had merely handled the
virus well enough for the U.S. to have the

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:05.330
same not not number of cases, but mortality
rate of other wealthy countries at our level

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:06.940
of development.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:12.170
This study was published in The Lancet, one
of the oldest and best known medical journals,

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:22.190
and it explains that the U.S. had way more
deaths, a higher mortality rate during the

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:29.659
pandemic than other rich countries, countries,
including the UK and a number of other countries,

00:01:29.659 --> 00:01:32.810
and that many of the cases and deaths were
avoidable.

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:36.880
They could have been avoided by the federal
government response being more serious from

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.740
the beginning, rolling out testing earlier
on, having stricter guidelines or at least

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:45.550
making it clear that they should be enforced
and that Donald Trump wanted to see those

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:46.630
enforced.

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:51.409
And unfortunately, some of these problems
date back even before Donald Trump.

00:01:51.409 --> 00:01:54.860
We know that the United States, when it comes
to health care, even though we spend a ton

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:59.530
of money on health care, we often have worse
outcomes than many other wealthy developed

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:03.680
countries, Germany, Canada, UK, so on and
so forth.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:07.170
And so part of this is a bigger problem than
Donald Trump.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:12.751
A lot of our systems not interacting well,
federal and state not interacting well, so

00:02:12.751 --> 00:02:14.300
on and so forth.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.660
But then beyond that was the failed federal
response from Donald Trump.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:20.080
And I think a lot of us intuitively understand
this.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:25.400
The number of infections early, the lack of
just being realistic, the lack of letting

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.870
actual medical professionals guide the response.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:33.060
And as I've said before, if indeed Donald
and we'll talk about this in a moment when

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:38.400
we talk about Joe Biden's approval rating,
if Donald Trump had simply said, what do doctors

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.440
think we should do, what do public health
experts think we should do?

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:46.480
Epidemiologists, immunologists, people who
know about this and aren't going to say things

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:50.920
like, would the flu vaccine work against coronavirus,
as Donald Trump did back in?

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:56.090
I don't remember if it was February or March,
many of these deaths would have been avoided.

00:02:56.090 --> 00:03:00.760
And we now know that beyond any doubt whatsoever.

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:07.420
And the question now becomes, under new leadership,
can we do as well as other countries when

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:13.459
it comes to vaccine distribution and lowering
the mortality rate and keeping cases low if

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:14.730
and when we get them low?

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:18.060
So far, the numbers are cautiously optimistic.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:23.020
We had a couple of days in the last week where
there were two million vaccinations done each

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:24.020
day.

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:27.390
If indeed we have a third vaccine approved
sometime in the near future, as it looks like

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:31.810
we will, it's not completely unreasonable
to think that we could get to a steady two

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:35.430
or 2.5 million vaccine doses per day.

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:36.950
And we.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:42.720
These are not, you know, one of the saddest
things that has taken place during the pandemic.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:47.880
Obviously the deaths and cases and economic
implications and psychological impact for

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:50.470
so many people have been terrible.

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:56.790
But one of the saddest things that that we've
also seen has been the realization that the

00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:02.090
people in charge really do make a difference
what the politics are of your governor in

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:03.379
dealing with the pandemic.

00:04:03.379 --> 00:04:05.180
It really makes a difference.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:09.080
Whether there is a competent federal government
response really makes a difference when you

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:14.410
have people like Jared Kushner saying while
the stockpile is our stockpile, it's not for

00:04:14.410 --> 00:04:15.849
the states.

00:04:15.849 --> 00:04:20.829
That's just not a disgusting political statement
that you see on TV that has a real trickle

00:04:20.829 --> 00:04:22.049
down impact.

00:04:22.049 --> 00:04:24.479
And hopefully we're going to see that improve.

00:04:24.479 --> 00:04:28.099
And it seems as though the American people
are confident that it is improving.

00:04:28.099 --> 00:04:32.419
Joe Biden with the highest initial approval
rating in twenty eight years.

00:04:32.419 --> 00:04:50.499
Let's talk about 

00:04:50.499 --> 00:05:54.160
that now.

